[ledge] The six flat counterbore floors are the M3 socket-head bearing faces. Their 5.8 mm diameter and depth seat the selected screw heads below the exterior face; these retained hardware seats require flat head contact.
alternatives: Sloping the floors removes the screw-head bearing plane. Filling the counterbores makes the heads project into the 0.4 mm gap beneath the foam cap.
